From b192fc29d662c2ada3fc9d9a944a20486ba4eff5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Niedermayer <michael@niedermayer.cc>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 22:44:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] avformat/rtpdec_rfc4175: Return the recovered frame with its
 own timestamp

When a packet of the next frame ended a frame whose marker was
missed, that frame was returned with the timestamp of the next frame.

This is not a security issue.

Fixes: Gcg4mf6RNmEA
Wrong timestamp Replicated through API
Found-by: Forgejo Fairy while reviewing PR #24949
(cherry picked from commit b192fc29d662c2ada3fc9d9a944a20486ba4eff5)
---
 libavformat/rtpdec_rfc4175.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libavformat/rtpdec_rfc4175.c b/libavformat/rtpdec_rfc4175.c
index 32b09ae80b9..cbb1afd050c 100644
--- a/libavformat/rtpdec_rfc4175.c
+++ b/libavformat/rtpdec_rfc4175.c
@@ -269,7 +269,10 @@ static int rfc4175_handle_packet(AVFormatContext *ctx, PayloadContext *data,
         if (!data->frame)
             data->frame = av_mallocz(data->frame_size + AV_INPUT_BUFFER_PADDING_SIZE);
 
-        data->timestamp = *timestamp;
+        if (missed_last_packet)
+            FFSWAP(uint32_t, data->timestamp, *timestamp);
+        else
+            data->timestamp = *timestamp;
 
         if (!data->frame) {
             av_log(ctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "Out of memory.\n");
-- 
2.53.0

